==Evolution==
Evolves Into '''Coppermine, type κ''' at level 10.

Evolves Into '''Divine Coppermine κ''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Before True Form, Coppermine is pretty much useless due to her poor stats and range, and because the spammability of [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]] and [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] heavily outclasses her in terms of stalling Floating enemies.

One of the few redeeming qualities of Coppermine is her stackability (66.20 seconds is a great recharge time for an Uber such as her). Stacking Coppermines is quite easy thanks to her good range, decent health, and short recharge, and a stack of Coppermines can deal surprisingly great DPS.

If you're going to use Coppermine, make sure to capitalize on her [[Freeze]] ability with the [[Cat Combo]] [[Smiles at Cats (Combo)|Smiles at Cats]], which requires only her and the [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Basic Cat]].

==='''True Form'''===
Divine Coppermine κ has 5,343 DPS, which is quite decent for a unit with her recharge time and attack range. Additionally, her improved attack range (410) allows her to remain behind the frontlines, while safely dealing good damage to enemies. And her chance of freezing Floating enemies has now increased to 75%! Unfortunately, none of this change anything about her significantly, as a stack of Necro-Dancer Cats can achieve the exact same thing (minus the Area Attack and DPS), with more reliability.

==='''Talents'''===
Sadly, none of Coppermine's Talents bring much improvement.

'''Attack Buff''' is her most worthwhile Talent if you're intending on investing in her Ultra Talents; otherwise it sees little use, as Coppermine's damage is of little consequence in most situations.

Similarly, '''HP Buff''' can be decent in the same way that Attack Buff is with her Ultra Talents, but is not very useful on a backliner such as her. Coppermine is more keen on outranging enemies regardless of investment level.

'''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Wave]]''' can give her potential counterplay against bad [[Bun Bun Symbiote]] RNG or in stages with [[Pigeon de Sable]], but even then it hardly ever comes into play and should be avoided, as with all Resist Talents.

'''Cost Down''' is the only other Talent you should consider investing in, as it is a visible improvement, albeit a small one.

'''Resist Slow''' is nigh-useless on her, so avoid it.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
Divine Coppermine κ gets 6 Ultra Talents, those being a guaranteed level 3 '''[[Surge Attack#Mini-Surge|Mini-Surge]]''', '''Attack Frequency Up''' by 50%, '''Target Zombie''', '''Strong Against''', '''Zombie Killer''', and '''HP Buff Up''' by 50%, all 6 of which, thankfully, do a very good job at giving her some much needed utility.

'''Attack Frequency Up''' is a bit deceptive at first glance. Despite only shaving off 0.77 seconds from her attack rate, her TBA is already lightning-quick, providing noticeably better utility despite its hefty cost. This is still the lowest-priority Ultra Talent of the bunch, and should only be considered after unlocking the following.

What really sells Coppermine is her '''Mini-Surge''' ability, which, at Lv.60 with max Attack Buff Talents, gives Coppermine an average DPS of 19,300 against all enemies (22,000 with Attack Frequency Up), assuming all hits land.

The Mini-Surge itself also has good qualities outside of simply more offense. It has the ability to linger outside her range and serve as piercing damage, which also extends her uptime. This makes Coppermine significantly better as both an offensive and supportive unit. The only thing that can be a problem is her spawn range, but her mobility and quick attacks can make this a nuisance at worst, and a positive attribute at best.

Coppermine's next Ultra Talent is '''Target Zombie''', giving her another niche to strive in, specifically one with less competition. Just like her previous anti-Floating superiors, [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Weedwacker]] and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife]] don't immediately invalidate her usage. Despite not having Zombie Killer, Coppermine's mobility, DPS, and Freeze uptime are useful when she can counter a majority of melee Zombies with relative ease. Running her with [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] is highly recommended to pick off any corpses if you intend on unlocking this Ultra Talent.

'''Strong Against''' and '''HP Buff +''' both help with her survivability outside of outranging, with strong also giving her a whopping 32k dps against floating and zombies.

Speaking about zombies, '''Zombie Killer''' is a nice final addition to Coppermine's kit, as now she can properly deal with zombies.

Even with all of this, what Coppermine provides is simply not worth the gargantuan investment needed to turn a mediocre Uber into a competent crowd-controller/DPS, especially by the point of progression this would be unlocked in. Nonetheless, she does improve dramatically with these Ultra Talents, making the price tag potentially justifiable if you truly wish to upgrade her capabilities against volatile endgame targets like [[Mini White Cyclone]] or [[Oldstrich]] (despite their Freeze resistance).

