==Trivia==
*She was added to the game alongside [[Kuu (Uber Rare Cat)|Kuu]] and [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Kai]] on May 14th, 2014.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Coppermine was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Journey to the West (Removed Combo)|Journey to the West]].
*Prior to [[Version 12.7 Update|Version 12.7]], Divine Coppermine κ's Attack Frequency Up [[Talents|Ultra Talent]] reduced her time between attacks by 4f <sup>0.13s</sup> per level up to 40f <sup>1.33s</sup>, considerably longer than the amount of idle time which can be reduced from her attack cycle (23f <sup>0.77s</sup>). This meant that upgrades past level 6 had no practical impact unless she was knocked back during her backswing. She along with [[Anubis the Protector (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Anubis]] were the only units affected by this excessive progression before this version.
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], Coppermine's English True Form name lacked the "κ" part.
*Prior to [[Version 15.4 Update|Version 15.4]], Coppermine's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Coppermine
Magicial beauty powered by her staff
Releases beams of light (Area Attack)
Might freeze floating enemies.</pre>
<pre>Coppermine, type κ
Doesn't smile that often. (Area Attack)
In front of cats, however.. different story.
Might stop floating enemies.</pre>
<pre>Divine Coppermine κ
What can you do for her that her favorite
Cat doesn't already? Come back in 100
years, kid. Might stop Floating (Area Attack)</pre>
**Some notable typos were that "Magical" was misspelled as "Magic'''i'''al" in her Normal Form's description, "Cats" wasn't capitalized in her Evolved Form's description, and that "[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]]" wasn't capitalized in either of her first two Forms' descriptions. Her True Form's description also referred to the [[Freeze]] ability by its old name, "stop".
*Divine Coppermine κ's description contains a typo, in that "Area attack" is singular and not plural.
*Divine Coppermine κ was among the first Uber Rare Cats to receive an extra set of Ultra Talents, and by extension, the [[Special Abilities#Stat Enhancements|HP Buff+]] ability.
*The "κ" in her Evolved Form is the Greek letter "kappa".
**Coppermine's Japanese name, romanized as ''Kappāmain'', begins with the same sound as the Greek letter.
*Coppermine is loosely based on [[wikipedia:Sha Wujing|Sha Wujing]] from ''[[wikipedia:Journey to the West|Journey to the West]]''. Her weapon is modeled after a [[wikipedia:Monk's spade|monk's spade]], a trait commonly found in Wujing's portrayal. The skull designs on her staff are a reference to the necklace of monk skulls that Wujing wore. Her hair colour substitutes the blue skin that Wujing is sometimes depicted as having. The plate above her head is commonly found in Japanese portrayals of Wujing, as he is usually treated as a ''[[wikipedia:Kappa (folklore)|kappa]]'', which also has a plate on its head.
**Interestingly, [[Kappy Jr.]] and [[Kappy Kawano]] also exist and reference the ''kappa'', but there is no correlation between the three's descriptions.
*Coppermine is a reference to [[Mari Illustrious (Super Rare Cat)|Mari Illustrious]] from ''[[wikipedia:Rebuild of Evangelion|Rebuild of Evangelion]]'', as described in [[Nyanko Ecology Report Large Edition]]. Her suit even looks like the "plugsuits" worn by [[EVA Unit-08 (Uber Rare Cat)|Evangelion]] pilots.
**Coincidentally, Mari, alongside her [[EVA Unit-08 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA unit]] and [[Mari Cat (Rare Cat)|Cat equivalent]] are all dedicated [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] units, the same as Coppermine prior to being given Ultra Talents. Mari Illustrious also has [[Immune to Freeze|Freeze Immunity]], something that Coppermine gains in her True Form.
*On release, a sprite of Coppermine's left hand was mistakenly placed behind her left arm, leaving an empty space between her forearm and staff during the parts of her animations where it was intended to be used. The fingertips from it also overlapped with a sprite of her right foot, although they were only faintly visible during her attack animation.
*Coppermine's Normal Form Upgrade Menu icon shows a line below her earpiece that doesn't belong to anything seen in-game. Moreover, her Evolved Form's icons both show a round object near her left shoulder that's also missing from her finalized appearance, with a second appearing where the line from before was in her Upgrade Menu icon.
*The event poster for the [[AIR BUSTERS (Gacha Event)|AIR BUSTERS]] banner has a typo in the text describing Coppermine's ability, saying that she can "Stop Floating enemies dead '''on''' their tracks!", instead of "...dead '''in''' their tracks!". The [[Cyber Academy Galaxy Gals (Gacha Event)|Galaxy Gals]] poster also had this typo, but it was eventually fixed in the tenth iteration of it.
*The Cat face on Coppermine, type κ's staff was originally intended to have some eye shine, but this detail was effectively removed when her sprites were compressed.
**A couple details on Divine Coppermine κ's gear met the same fate; her staff's Cat face was supposed to have the eyes of a [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]], while her earpieces used to have ridges along their lower portions. The latter of the two is however visible in her Upgrade Menu icon, though only partially.
*In [[The Battle Cats POP!]], Coppermine is the only Galaxy Gal to have all of her facial animations left intact.

